-- title:
--   Soundness of an octant projection check
-- statement:
--   Let $c,o$ be configurations, $\sigma=(o.a-o.b)/o.q$, $t=c.t_n/2^{c.t_q}$,
--   $K,N,p,r_n,r_d,F_n,F_d\in\mathbb N$, and $s=\sigma+it$. Let accumulator lists
--   $x_1,x_2$ satisfy the defined list enclosure predicates for the partial-sum
--   weights after $N-1$ and $N$ terms. If the defined $\operatorname{checkOct}$
--   returns true for integer octant $j$, put $r=r_n/r_d$, $F=F_n/F_d$ and let
--   $X_j,A_j,B_j$ be the defined octant projection and integer coefficients. Then
--   $$\sum_{k=1}^p\frac{|X_j(W_k(K,N,s))|r^k}{k!}
--   +(|A_j|+|B_j|)F<X_j(W_0(K,N,s)).$$
--   All quotients use Lean's total real division.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/H1000Octant.lean#L530-L638

